{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Laravel 12 Controller Creation Workflow",
  "description": "Controller creation with Form Request validation and Laravel 12 conventions",
  "version": "2.0",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileCreated",
    "patterns": ["app/Http/Controllers/*.php"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A new controller has been created! Please guide through Laravel 12 controller best practices:\n\n1. **Form Requests**: Create validation classes with `php artisan make:request Store{ModelName}Request` and `php artisan make:request Update{ModelName}Request`\n2. **Type Declarations**: Use explicit return type declarations for all methods\n3. **Thin Controllers**: Keep controllers thin by delegating business logic to services\n4. **HTTP Status Codes**: Use proper HTTP status codes for responses\n5. **API Resources**: Create API resources if needed with `php artisan make:resource {ModelName}Resource`\n6. **Authorization**: Add proper authorization with policies and gates\n7. **Route Model Binding**: Use route model binding for cleaner code\n\nRun `vendor/bin/pint --dirty` to format the new controller."
  }
}